WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:01.790
- [Narrator] This Great
Big Story was made possible

00:00:01.790 --> 00:00:06.563
by Wells Fargo, established
1852, re-established 2018.

00:00:07.701 --> 00:00:10.220
When it comes to horror movies,

00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:13.380
there's an actor who
is so good at his job,

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:15.110
his performances stay with you

00:00:15.110 --> 00:00:17.623
like a nightmare you
just can't wake up from,

00:00:18.470 --> 00:00:21.528
but trust us, he's a really nice guy.

00:00:21.528 --> 00:00:24.558
(sinister music)

00:00:24.558 --> 00:00:26.950
- [Interviewer] Could you give us a clap?

00:00:26.950 --> 00:00:28.230
- Let's go.

00:00:28.230 --> 00:00:29.847
I'm Javier Botet, and I'm an actor.

00:00:29.847 --> 00:00:33.090
- [Narrator] And Javier's
been in a lot of movies,

00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:34.690
you probably just didn't see him

00:00:34.690 --> 00:00:38.010
because, well, he looks quite
different most of the time.

00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:41.910
- I feel very comfortable
in monster roles,

00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:45.950
I've been in "It," "Mama," "Conjuring 2,"

00:00:45.950 --> 00:00:48.017
"Crimson Peak," "Slender Man."

00:00:48.017 --> 00:00:49.330
- [Narrator] And let's not forget,

00:00:49.330 --> 00:00:51.363
he's been in "The Mummy" and "Alien," too.

00:00:52.330 --> 00:00:54.980
- I'm very skinny; I'm two meters tall

00:00:54.980 --> 00:00:58.700
and 56 kilograms.

00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:02.300
It's not a problem of
eating, 'cause I love to eat;

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:06.363
it's a personal condition;
it's called Marfan Syndrome.

00:01:07.499 --> 00:01:08.972
- [Narrator] Javier's career started

00:01:08.972 --> 00:01:12.760
when he met a prosthetic
makeup teacher in Madrid.

00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:14.474
This led to Javier's first monster role

00:01:14.474 --> 00:01:17.400
in the movie, "Beneath Still Waters."

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:22.370
- That was my first makeup,
my first work in a real movie

00:01:22.370 --> 00:01:25.950
and, well, after that,
all the makeup artists

00:01:25.950 --> 00:01:29.975
start seeing my work and start
proposing me in other roles,

00:01:29.975 --> 00:01:32.190
and last year I'd been working

00:01:32.190 --> 00:01:35.406
in eight or nine different shows.

00:01:35.406 --> 00:01:36.697
- [Narrator] There's gotta be

00:01:36.697 --> 00:01:38.910
some behind-the-scenes gossip then?

00:01:38.910 --> 00:01:41.720
- Yeah, well, I was in Crimson Peak,

00:01:41.720 --> 00:01:44.400
I was out of all the makeup,

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:47.060
and I was the last day
with Guillermo del Toro,

00:01:47.060 --> 00:01:50.570
and I see Tom Hiddleston
and I say, "OK, see you,

00:01:50.570 --> 00:01:53.520
"it was a pleasure," and
he said, "Who are you?"

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:57.297
So I said, "I was your ex-wives."

00:01:57.297 --> 00:01:59.597
"Oh, OK, OK, OK ..."

00:01:59.597 --> 00:02:01.242
"Sorry, I didn't recognize you."

00:02:01.242 --> 00:02:03.470
- [Narrator] But don't
pigeonhole this guy.

00:02:03.470 --> 00:02:05.460
He might be a monster most of the time,

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:06.900
but he's got dramatic range.

00:02:06.900 --> 00:02:08.710
- OK, guys, are you ready?

00:02:08.710 --> 00:02:10.012
Really love what you do,

00:02:10.012 --> 00:02:13.210
'cause it's going to be
a hard and long journey.

00:02:13.210 --> 00:02:14.580
Be prepared,

00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:16.470
you never know what's gonna happen.

00:02:16.470 --> 00:02:20.233
Don't be shy; don't let
the fear paralyze you.

00:02:21.894 --> 00:02:23.293
So relax,

00:02:24.740 --> 00:02:26.461
you know what I mean?

00:02:26.461 --> 00:02:27.294
Woo!

00:02:27.294 --> 00:02:28.127
Whew!

00:02:28.127 --> 00:02:28.960
(laughing)

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:31.150
If I can ask for something,

00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:35.260
I would love to be a big Sith,

00:02:35.260 --> 00:02:38.662
I will rule the galaxy.

00:02:38.662 --> 00:02:42.329
(lasers firing and humming)

00:02:44.833 --> 00:02:48.046
- [Interviewer] That's amazing,
that's amazing, thank you.

00:02:48.046 --> 00:02:49.796
- [Javier] Thank you.

